    "title": "Field notes",
    "text": "K.O. Strohbehn watched a young mule deer buck cruising down the alley behind her house in East Jackson Aug. 26.\nPretty much the same visitors the past few weeks at Sue and John Hebberger, Jr.’s house: flocks of pine siskins, occasional juncos, passing crows and less frequently a nearby raven. Clark’s nutcrackers have been heard very nearby and one fleeting glimpse of a magpie — they continue to be most unusually absent. By way of mammals, red squirrels have made appearances, and the local mule deer doe with her pair of fawns regularly visit the Hebbergers’ yard and Sue’s flower beds.",
